{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqgrzywzw0q","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"Per-repo dashboard scoping: URL ?workspace= param + in-dashboard repo switcher","summary":"Decision (2026-06-16, user-owned): the orchestrator dashboard becomes per-repo via a ?workspace= URL param that drives the view (defaults to the current pinned state.workspace when absent, so existing /graph links keep working) PLUS an in-dashboard switcher dropdown listing every repo the daemon has seen. Chosen over (a) per-repo URL with no switcher and (b) switcher-only with no URL state, because URL+switcher is the back-compat superset: bookmarkable per repo AND live-switchable on one page. Root cause being fixed: the data layer is ALREADY per-workspace (every read route honors ?workspace=), but the single-page dashboard never threads the param, so it always renders the lone global state.workspace pointer — whichever repo's SessionStart hook pinged the daemon last (the documented workspace-gremlin at daemon.js:413). Accepted tradeoff: a global switcher enumerates all integrated repo paths to every dashboard (acceptable on a loopback-only bind). Net work is plumbing: persist a workspace registry + add GET /workspaces; extend /guidance to honor ?workspace= (it still uses buildGraph(state.workspace) at routes/session.js:16); thread workspace (+token when set) through every per-repo fetch in public/graph.html while leaving /health and /cron/usage global.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-16T15:07:17.507Z","vec":[-0.1318085491657257,-0.052917104214429855,-0.03757042437791824,0.02911785989999771,0.006278892979025841,-0.011670384556055069,0.026694253087043762,0.0015043796738609672,0.0066998121328651905,0.07109992206096649,-0.016390148550271988,-0.032929256558418274,0.007411588914692402,0.03347945958375931,-0.013536189682781696,0.0641031339764595,0.08402220904827118,-0.09421629458665848,0.012566648423671722,-0.0537828765809536,0.049652762711048126,-0.0725337490439415,-0.008009425364434719,0.003